w: 1.~Our Fa- ther, Thou in heav'n a- bove, Who bid- dest us to dwell in love, 
w: 2.~Thy name be hal- lowed. Help us, Lord, In pur- i- ty to keep Thy Word, 
w: 3.~Thy king- dom come. Thine let it be In time and in e- ter- ni- ty. 
w: 4.~Thy gra- cious will on earth be done As 'tis in heav'n be- fore Thy throne; 
w: 5.~Give us this day our dai- ly bread And let us all be clothed and fed. 
w: 6.~For- give our sins, Lord, we im- plore, Re- move from us their bur- den sore,
w: 7.~In- to temp- ta- tion lead us not. When e- vil foes a- gainst us plot
w: 8.~From e- vil, Lord, de- li- ver us; The times and days are per- il- ous.
